    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0249" n="237" xml:id="pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1881: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-01T14:00:00+02:00">June 1, 1942—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 1—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3037. The substance of Department’s telegram No. 2417, May 27, 9 p.m., with the
                    exception of the confidential paragraph<anchor n="11" xml:id="d256-f1"/> was
                    conveyed informally to the Foreign Office. Sir Maurice Peterson<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d256-f2"/> tells us that the British “will certainly do nothing” to
                    complicate matters in the light of our proposed voluntary offer of an American
                    military mission to the Iranian Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d256-f1" n="11" xml:id="d256-f1-content">
                <p>i.e., the third paragraph of the telegram.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d256-f2" n="12" xml:id="d256-f2-content">
                <p>British Ambassador temporarily in the Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
